/ PLang is an intent language: a quoted literal in a standard form is typed by that form, no `as`
/ needed. "2026-01-01" births a date, "PT30S" a duration; any other quoted text, a version-like
/ label under %version% among them, stays text. `as` is only a force.
BareLiteralJudgedByForm
- set %birthday% = "2026-01-01"
- assert %birthday!type.name% equals "date"
- set %timeout% = "PT30S"
- assert %timeout!type.name% equals "duration"
- set %version% = "2.0"
- assert %version!type.name% equals "text"
